<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.BlazorWebAssembly">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OverrideHtmlAssetPlaceholders>true</OverrideHtmlAssetPlaceholders>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    AR-1 stack choices, pinned centrally at 10.0.11. No Version attribute here - central
    package management forbids it.

    Corrected 2026-08-27: this comment previously read "Framework packages, not AR-1 stack
    choices ... rather than listed in the AR-1 table". That classification was a misreading of
    the source and was retracted in Directory.Packages.props and PackageVersionPinTests, which
    moved both packages into the asserted AR-1 pin set - epics.md lists "ASP.NET Core / Blazor
    WASM 10" under Pinned versions and the architecture spine gives it its own stack-table row.
    This file was the third of the three places and the only one left arguing the reversed
    reading. The chosen value was always right; the classification was not.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.DevServer" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    IStringLocalizer, added by story 1.3.

    A Blazor WebAssembly app resolves against Microsoft.NETCore.App and the WebAssembly packages
    rather than the ASP.NET Core shared framework, so this does not arrive for free the way it
    would in Yello.Host - verified against the restored asset graph, which contained no
    Microsoft.Extensions.Localization at all before this reference existed.

    It is not optional. `No_user_visible_string_literal_appears_in_a_component` fails the build
    on any word of two or more letters that is not `Yello` in a .razor text node, so a single
    `Email` label is a build failure - and the gate's own remedy message names
    `@Localizer["Key"]` as the idiom it expects. Pinned centrally as a non-AR-1 pin; see the
    comment in Directory.Packages.props.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Localization" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Yello.Contracts\Yello.Contracts.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Yello.Merge\Yello.Merge.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
